{
  "source_lines": [
    {
      "line_index": 0,
      "text": "Initially, patients were matched 1:2 based on gender, age, body mass index (BMI), and smoking history using pro-",
      "physical_page": 5,
      "assigned": true
    },
    {
      "line_index": 1,
      "text": "pensity scores to reduce confounding factors. After matching, Group 1 included 211 cases, and Group 2 included",
      "physical_page": 5,
      "assigned": true
    },
    {
      "line_index": 2,
      "text": "121 cases. There was no significant difference in the four features after matching. (Table 2) After matching, the two",
      "physical_page": 5,
      "assigned": true
    },
    {
      "line_index": 3,
      "text": "groups were subjected to univariate analysis, comparing features such as bronchial inflation signs, bubble signs,",
      "physical_page": 5,
      "assigned": true
    },
    {
      "line_index": 4,
      "text": "vascular convergence signs, lobulation signs, spiculation signs, pleural traction signs, CTR > 0.5, and the diameter of",
      "physical_page": 5,
      "assigned": true
    },
    {
      "line_index": 5,
      "text": "nodules. The results showed significant statistical differences between the two groups in the bronchus inflation sign",
      "physical_page": 5,
      "assigned": true
    },
    {
      "line_index": 6,
      "text": "(P < 0.001), vascular convergence sign (P < 0.001), lobulation sign (P < 0.001), spiculation sign (P < 0.001), pleural trac-",
      "physical_page": 5,
      "assigned": true
    },
    {
      "line_index": 7,
      "text": "tion sign (P = 0.001), CTR > 0.5 (P = 0.001), and the diameter of nodule (P < 0.001). These features were incorporated",
      "physical_page": 5,
      "assigned": true
    },
    {
      "line_index": 8,
      "text": "into the LASSO regression. (Fig. 2) The coefficients for the pleural traction sign and CTR > 0.5 were 0. (Table 3) After",
      "physical_page": 5,
      "assigned": true
    },
    {
      "line_index": 9,
      "text": "filtering, the remaining five features were used to construct a predictive model using binary Logistic regression. An",
      "physical_page": 5,
      "assigned": true
    },
    {
      "line_index": 10,
      "text": "ROC curve was plotted with an AUC of 0.785 and an accuracy of 0.726. Based on this predictive model, a nomogram",
      "physical_page": 5,
      "assigned": true
    },
    {
      "line_index": 11,
      "text": "was drawn. (Fig. 3).",
      "physical_page": 5,
      "assigned": true
    },
    {
      "line_index": 12,
      "text": "Table 3 Univariate and",
      "physical_page": 6,
      "assigned": true
    },
    {
      "line_index": 13,
      "text": "multivariate analysis between",
      "physical_page": 6,
      "assigned": true
    },
    {
      "line_index": 14,
      "text": "group 1 and group 2",
      "physical_page": 6,
      "assigned": true
    },
    {
      "line_index": 15,
      "text": "12.78(± 4.71)",
      "physical_page": 6,
      "assigned": true
    },
    {
      "line_index": 16,
      "text": "Fig. 3 Nomogram for predicting frozen section pathology upgrade",
      "physical_page": 6,
      "assigned": true
    }
  ],
